-- 22.sqm — record, on the pending row itself, which local one-time
-- pre-key its candidate was derived with. Upgrades schema 22 -> 23:
-- SQLDelight migration N.sqm runs when oldVersion <= N < newVersion.
--
-- Until now the binding was inferred at promotion time from
-- `opk_reservation.conversation_id`. That inference is correct only
-- while the invariant "at most one reservation per conversation, and
-- it backs the pending row" holds, and it cannot express the two
-- states a promotion must tell apart:
--
--   * this candidate owes a specific local key, and promoting it
--     without spending that key leaves the key republishable;
--   * this candidate used no local key at all (an OUTBOUND INITIATOR
--     pending: the `x3dhInit` in its artifacts names the PEER's pool),
--     and spending anything for it would destroy a live local key.
--
-- `opk_binding_known = 0` is neither of those: it means nothing wrote
-- a binding for this row. It must never be read as "no key was used".
--
-- Initiator artifacts identify a candidate derived without a local OPK.
-- Old responder rows have no durable key provenance. Even one reservation
-- with a matching timestamp is not a candidate identity, so these rows
-- remain Unknown until an authenticated bootstrap writes a new binding.
-- A headerless legacy candidate can therefore remain blocked after upgrade;
-- spending a guessed key or silently spending none is not a safe migration.

ALTER TABLE pending_ratchet_state ADD COLUMN opk_key_id_hex TEXT;

ALTER TABLE pending_ratchet_state ADD COLUMN opk_binding_known INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;

UPDATE pending_ratchet_state SET opk_binding_known = 1
WHERE bootstrap_artifacts_blob IS NOT NULL;
